# mtk/mt6768/drivers/input/conf: the MT6768's keys and its sensor hub.
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_<NAME>=y in a defconfig builds a driver into the kernel (docs/drivers-config.md). MediaTek's drivers are
# `default n`: a configuration has them only when it includes mt6768.config.

driver MTK_KEYS
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.mtk_keys.c
	default n
	help    the power and volume keys through the keypad at 0x10010000 and the PMIC's power key (buttons=2), and the clocks of
	help    the big cores (mtk_cpufreq=N) and of the Mali (mali_mhz=N, 375 to 950: GPUPLL, with VSRAM_GPU and VGPU set as
	help    MediaTek's table has them for that clock)

driver MTK_SCP
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.mtk_scp.c
	default n
	help    the SCP, the MT6768's sensor processor, started step by step (scp_step=N): its firmware's sensor hub, the
	help    accelerometer as kern.hakios.accel and the way up as kern.hakios.orientation_state (scp_step=7)

driver TCM
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.tcm.c
	default n
	help    the touch screen of the Infinix Hot 20 (x6826b): an OmniVision TD4160 on the MT6768's SPI2, TCM protocol
	help    (touchscreen=2); mtkloader sends it its firmware (fw-touch/) before the kernel starts. The bus and pins are
	help    that phone's; another MT6768 phone with this controller changes those
